This week was my last week in Gobo =F0=9F=91=80
Now I'm in Nishiwaki! It's double the population, and we even have a friend
on Baptismal Date =F0=9F=98=AE SPEAKING OF WHICH!

In my last lesson with Elder Childs and Jian, we invited him to baptism,
and he said yes =F0=9F=8E=8A Jian will be baptized on the 4th of April. Sup=
er
exciting!

Another cool thing from this last week in Gobo was getting to give a
priesthood blessing to Sister Kuwata in Japanese. She was feeling poorly
and called us up for a blessing. We both had to learn unfamiliar Japanese
vocabulary, but it was really spiritual.

Now that I'm in Nishiwaki, I'm companions with Elder Talbot. He's really
chill and a calm dude so it's gonna be fun to work with him!

One thing I focused on this past week was looking at those around me as the
Savior would. It's really hard to try and treat everyone the way that He
would, but we can learn so much from it.

There's nobody you hate, nobody that you view as less talented, there isn't
ant kind of preconception based on appearance or situation.

It's only reaching out in love, and with Christlike confidence. We can be
confident if we know our actions are backed by Charity, Christlike love.

I love you guys! Perhaps not like the Savior, but I'm trying my best. I
wish you all the best!!

Here's a few pictures from this past week too!

